      "name": "PlayBinkVideoFile",
      "signature": "dword * PlayBinkVideoFile(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword *",
      "comment": "PlayBinkVideoFile - Initialize and display Bink video playback with message loop\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize bink display surface type and sound system\n2. Determine expansion flag to set file search scope (4 or 5)\n3. Open Bink video file from disk using SFileOpenFileEx\n4. Initialize Bink video context with _BinkOpen\n5. Calculate video frame dimensions and stride alignment\n6. Enter main message loop with 500ms timeout\n7. Process Windows messages (keyboard/mouse/close events)\n8. For each valid frame: lock video surface, render frame, unlock surface\n9. Update frame counter and check for completion\n10. Clean up Bink context and file handle\n11. Validate DirectX 3+ capability\n12. Query registry for display device configuration\n13. Return status code or fallback device settings\n\nParameters:\n- (implicit) in_ECX: Bink video filename to play\n- (implicit) in_EDX: surface type parameter (1-4 range, maps to DirectDraw surface types)\n- (implicit) global DAT_6f8f1bac: Render surface interface pointer\n- (implicit) global DAT_6f8f1bd0: Critical section for synchronization\n\nReturns:\n- 0x1: Success - video played to completion or device validation passed\n- 0x0: Failure - file not found or Bink initialization failed\n- NULL: Expansion flag check or critical section assertion failed\n\nSpecial Cases:\n- Surface type mapping: EDI param 1-4 maps through switch table to DirectDraw enums\n- Alignment: frame width rounded up to next multiple of 4\n- Timeout: 500ms from first frame render to completion\n- Critical section: protects surface access during frame copying\n- Search scope: expansion flag changes file search directory\n\nControl Flow:\n- Early exits: no Bink file found, Bink initialization failed\n- Main loop: processes messages until timeout or user closes window\n- Error paths: FogAssert for assertions, cleanup before return\n\nGlobals Modified:\n- DAT_6f8f1120: Bink context handle (allocated/freed)\n- DAT_6f8f112c: Completion flag (set to 1 when video completes)\n- DAT_6f8f1130: User abort flag (set to 1 on close/key/mouse)\n- DAT_6f8f1134: Tick count when abort triggered\n- DAT_6f8f1128: DirectDraw surface type result\n- DAT_6f8f1118: Frame width in pixels (aligned)\n- DAT_6f8f111c: Frame height in pixels\n- DAT_6f8f153c: Flag to skip frame rendering\n- DAT_6f8f1674: Device name string (max 256 bytes)\n- DAT_6f8f1660: Device flags from registry\n- DAT_6f8f1664: Device capabilities (4 bytes)\n- DAT_6f8f1b90: DirectX version validation flag\n\nMagic Numbers:\n- 0x4 (default search scope - no expansion)\n- 0x5 (search scope with expansion)\n- 0x1a (26 dwords to clear - buffer size)\n- 0x64 (method offset for frame lock, offset 0x64 in vtable)\n- 0x80 (method offset for surface unlock, offset 0x80 in vtable)\n- 0x100 (256 byte buffer for registry device name)\n- 0x10 (16 byte registry query size)\n- 0x1f4 (500 in decimal - timeout milliseconds)\n- 0x3 (mask for alignment check)\n\nError Handling:\n- Missing file: returns NULL after log message \"...Couldn't l...\"\n- Bink init: closes file and returns NULL after log message \"BinkOpen failed...\"\n- Bink render: returns NULL, handled before assertion\n- No critical section: jumps to assertion\n- No expansion flag: assertion triggers\n\nDevice Detection Logic:\n- Queries registry for \"Diablo II VideoConfig\" settings\n- Reads device name, flags, and capabilities\n- Validates against gdwBitMasks\n- Falls back to \"Fallback DirectDraw Device\" if registry missing\n- Validates DirectX version and device capabilities",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
