      "name": "FlushDirectDrawRender",
      "signature": "dword FlushDirectDrawRender(void)",
      "calling_convention": "__stdcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Flushes pending DirectDraw render output to display during cleanup.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Check g_dwColorBitDepth: if 0 (palettized mode), execute color-mode path\n  2. Color-mode (palettized): copy primary to render surface via BltFast (offset 0x1c)\n  3. Color-mode errors: log \"BltFast failed\" with return code, exit with failure (0)\n  4. Non-palettized mode: validate render and primary surfaces not equal\n  5. Non-palettized: copy via secondary surface BltFast (offset 0x1c)\n  6. Call primary surface virtual method at offset 0x2c (Flip or similar)\n  7. Check DAT_6f8f1bd4 flag: if set, clear and call SetEntries\n  8. SetEntries parameters: 0x1, 0xff (full palette), data at 0x6f8f178c\n  9. SetEntries errors: log \"SetEntries failed\" with return code, exit failure (0)\n  10. Success return: 1\n\nParameters:\n  None\n\nReturns:\n  1 (success): Render output flushed successfully to display\n  0 (failure): BltFast or SetEntries error occurred (code logged)\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Palettized mode (g_dwColorBitDepth==0) requires primary and render surfaces\n  - Non-palettized requires secondary surface (g_ddSurfaceDesc) distinct from primary\n  - Palette updates (DAT_6f8f1bd4) only attempted when primary DirectDraw object available\n  - Called 3 times consecutively in DirectDraw cleanup loop before surface release",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:fe3522a376af59d3d3a491bb292b40f3",
