      "name": "CopyBufferData",
      "signature": "void CopyBufferData(uint * pSrcBuffer)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Copies 0x48 (72) DWORD values from source buffer to global buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Initialize destination pointer to g_aBuffer\n  2. Loop 0x48 (72) times:\n     - Copy DWORD from source to destination\n     - Increment both pointers\n  3. Set g_pCurrentBuffer to point to copied buffer\n  4. Return\n\nParameters:\n  pSrcBuffer (ECX): Pointer to source data array (72 DWORDs)\n\nReturns:\n  void (no return value)\n\nNotes:\n  Uses REP MOVSD for efficient copying\n  Destination is fixed global buffer at 0x6f8f1540\n  Also updates tracking pointer g_pCurrentBuffer",
