      "comment": "Creates a bitmap table for all ASCII printable characters (0x20-0x7f) for font rendering.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Create device context for DISPLAY and font (Courier, 10pt)\n  2. Create 8x16 bitmap and select into device context\n  3. Set text color (foreground) and background (DAT_6f8f1ed8)\n  4. For each character 0x20 (32) to 0x7f (127):\n     a. Draw character on bitmap\n     b. Scan bitmap 8x16 pixels: sample pixel color with GetPixel\n     c. If matches text color, store 0xFF (foreground), else 0x00 (background)\n     d. Store character offset in g_aCharacterOffsets array (0x80 bytes per char)\n  5. Get character widths for 0x20-0x7f and store in g_aCharacterWidths\n  6. Clean up: delete bitmap, font, device context\n\nParameters:\n  (none - no parameters)\n\nReturns:\n  void (results stored in globals: g_pFontBitmapTable, g_aCharacterOffsets, g_aCharacterWidths)\n\nNote: Creates 0x3000 (12288) byte buffer for bitmap data via FogMemAlloc\n      Each character: 8 pixels wide x 16 pixels tall = 128 bytes per char",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
