      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Draws a filled rectangle to the render surface buffer\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Call GetRenderMode() to get render surface pointer and validate render mode\n  2. Load screen dimensions from global variables (g_dwScreenHeight, g_dwScreenWidth)\n  3. Clamp all coordinates to valid screen bounds [0, max_x] x [0, max_y]\n  4. Early exit if rectangle is degenerate (y1 == y2 or x1 == x2)\n  5. Calculate destination buffer pointer: base + (y1 * screen_stride) + x1\n  6. Select rendering path based on nRenderMode value:\n     - Mode 1: Copy palette-indexed bytes directly\n     - Mode 2: Apply palettized blending via lookup table indirection\n     - Other modes: Solid fill with color byte, using DWORD-aligned REP STOSD\n  7. For each scanline, update row pixels and advance pointer by screen height stride\n\nParameters:\n  nX1: Top-left X coordinate (input, may exceed bounds, clamped to [0, screen_width-1])\n  nY1: Top-left Y coordinate (input, may exceed bounds, clamped to [0, screen_height-1])\n  nX2: Bottom-right X coordinate (input, may exceed bounds, clamped to [0, screen_width-1])\n  nY2: Bottom-right Y coordinate (input, may exceed bounds, clamped to [0, screen_height-1])\n  dwColor: Color/palette value (input, low byte is palette index or solid color value)\n  nRenderMode: Rendering mode selector (input, 1=copy, 2=blend, other=solid fill)\n\nReturns:\n  None (void), function modifies render surface buffer in place. Returns immediately if\n  coordinates are invalid or degenerate. Asserts on y-coordinate overflow detection.",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:ae9609438a3c35f80bd06c4b89002372",
