      "name": "FillClippedRectangle",
      "signature": "void FillClippedRectangle(int * pRect)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Fills a clipped rectangle with a solid color.\n\nAlgorithm:\n  1. Validate input rectangle left < right and top < bottom\n  2. Clip rectangle to screen bounds [0, g_dwScreenWidth) x [0, g_dwScreenHeight)\n  3. If clipped rectangle is empty, return\n  4. Calculate stride and fill entire rectangle row by row\n  5. Use STOSD/STOSB for optimized color fill (replicate byte color to all 4 bytes)\n\nParameters:\n  pRect: Pointer to rectangle structure containing [left, top, right, bottom] as 32-bit ints\n  DL: Color byte to fill with (replicated across all 4 bytes when filling as DWORD)\n\nReturns:\n  void\n\nSpecial Cases:\n  - Asserts if left >= right or top >= bottom before clipping\n  - Silently clips to [0, g_dwScreenWidth) x [0, g_dwScreenHeight)\n  - Does nothing if clipped rectangle is empty or has zero area\n  - Uses high-speed STOSD (fill as DWORD) for 4-byte chunks, STOSB for remainder",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "STR",
      "index": "STR:660b70fb93d7a717da5d6826022cc00d",
