      "name": "GetBufferFieldValue",
      "signature": "dword GetBufferFieldValue(int nFieldIndex, dword * pOutValue)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Returns a field value from the current buffer by index.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Look up field offset from lookup table g_pFieldLookupTable using nFieldIndex as key\n2. Read value at that offset from g_pCurrentBuffer\n3. Store value in output pointer pOutValue\n4. Use jump table dispatch (0-6) to return specific buffer fields\n\nParameters:\n- nFieldIndex (ECX): Field index (0-6 valid, 7+ returns 0)\n- pOutValue (EDX): Output pointer to store looked-up value\n\nReturns:\n- EAX: Field value from g_pCurrentBuffer at computed offset\n  - Cases 0-6: Corresponding buffer field values\n  - Default (index > 6): 0\n\nStructure Layout (g_pCurrentBuffer offsets):\n- Offset 0x0: Field 2 (case 0)\n- Offset 0x4: Field 1 (case 1)\n- Offset 0x8: Field 0 (case 2)\n- Offset 0x104: Field 3 (case 3)\n- Offset 0x108: Field 4 (case 4)\n- Offset 0x10c: Field 6 (case 6)\n\nNote: Jump table dispatch at 0x6f8e43ae selects return value path based on nFieldIndex",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
