      "sizes": {
        "LoD/1.07": 274,
        "LoD/1.08": 274,
        "LoD/1.09": 274,
        "LoD/1.09b": 274,
        "LoD/1.09d": 274,
        "LoD/1.10": 274
      },
      "name": "RenderCelFrameWithBoundaryCheck",
      "signature": "dword RenderCelFrameWithBoundaryCheck(CelFile * pCelFile)",
      "calling_convention": "__fastcall",
      "return_type": "dword",
      "comment": "Render a CEL frame to screen with boundary checking and blend mode support.\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Load or retrieve CEL frame data for the file\n2. Extract CEL file information (table index, mode, height)\n3. Validate vertical boundaries: Y + height must fit within screen bounds\n4. Validate horizontal boundaries: X + width - mode offset must fit within screen bounds\n5. Resolve blend/color buffer based on blend mode index (0-6, default=0)\n6. If palette index mask (0xFF) is not 0xFF, add palette offset from buffer[offset+3]\n7. If blend mode is 7, override with special palette from buffer[0x46]\n8. Call D2CMP_DecodeAndDrawCelFrame with computed parameters\n9. Return 1 on success, 0 on boundary violation or data load failure\n\nParameters:\n- pCelFile (ECX): Pointer to CelFile structure containing image data\n- nScreenY (implicit in EDX): Y coordinate on screen\n- nScreenX (implicit in stack): X coordinate on screen\n- nBlendMode (stack): Blend/color buffer mode index (0-7)\n- wPaletteIndex (stack): Palette index and mask byte (0xFF = use default)\n- dwFlags (stack): Additional rendering flags passed to decode function\n\nReturns:\n- 1: Frame rendered successfully within bounds\n- 0: Failed to load frame data or boundary violation detected\n\nBoundary Checks:\n- Vertical: (Y + CelHeight) < ScreenHeight AND (X + CelTableIndex + Y) >= -1\n- Horizontal: (CelWidth + X) >= -1 AND (CelWidth + X - CelMode) < ScreenWidth\n\nBlend Mode Selection (from g_pCurrentBuffer):\n- Mode 0: g_pCurrentBuffer[2] (standard blend)\n- Mode 1: g_pCurrentBuffer[1] (alternate blend)\n- Mode 2: g_pCurrentBuffer[0] (base color)\n- Mode 3: g_pCurrentBuffer[0x41] (extended color 1)\n- Mode 4: g_pCurrentBuffer[0x42] (extended color 2)\n- Mode 5: (default 0) - No color override\n- Mode 6: g_pCurrentBuffer[0x43] (extended color 3)\n- Mode 7: g_pCurrentBuffer[0x46] (special palette)",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:020c6d8da20fe7cb705e78fc12d7e861",
