      "name": "ParseStringToExtendedFloat",
      "signature": "void ParseStringToExtendedFloat(char * lpszDigitString, int nDigitCount, dword * pResult)",
      "calling_convention": "__cdecl",
      "return_type": "void",
      "comment": "Converts a string of digits into extended precision floating-point format\n\nAlgorithm:\n1. Initialize 96-bit result buffer to zero and set initial exponent to 0x404e\n2. If input string has digits, process each character:\n   - Save current 96-bit state (dwDigitValue, dwMid, dwHi) \n   - Perform three left shifts to multiply by 8\n   - Add saved state back (multiply by 9 total)\n   - Perform one more left shift (multiply by 10 total)\n   - Clear intermediate values and get next digit value\n   - Add digit value to 96-bit accumulator\n   - Advance to next character and decrement counter\n3. Normalize result by shifting away leading zeros:\n   - While high word is zero, shift 16 bits left and subtract 0x10 from exponent\n   - While bit 15 of high word is clear, shift 1 bit left and subtract 1 from exponent\n4. Store final exponent as 16-bit value at offset +10 in result structure\n\nParameters:\nlpszDigitString - Input string containing decimal digits to parse\nnDigitCount - Number of characters to process from input string\npResult - Pointer to 96-bit extended precision result buffer\n\nReturns:\nvoid (result stored in pResult buffer)\n\nSpecial Cases:\nIf nDigitCount is 0, result is initialized to zero with default exponent\n\nMagic Numbers Reference:\n0x404e - Initial exponent value (16462 decimal), represents bias for extended precision\n0xfff0 - Exponent adjustment (-16) for 16-bit left shifts during normalization\n0xffff - Exponent adjustment (-1) for single-bit left shifts during normalization\n0x8000 - Bit mask (32768) to test bit 15 for normalization completion\n\nExtended Precision Layout:\nOffset  Size  Field Name    Type      Description\n+0      4     dwLow         dword     Low 32 bits of 96-bit mantissa\n+4      4     dwMid         dword     Middle 32 bits of 96-bit mantissa  \n+8      4     dwHigh        dword     High 32 bits of 96-bit mantissa\n+10     2     wExponent     word      16-bit exponent with bias\n\nAlgorithm Verification:\nStep 2 multiplication: (value * 8) + value + (result * 2) = value * 10\nStep 3 normalization ensures bit 15 of high word is set for consistent format",
      "name_source": "LoD/1.07",
      "method": "CAL",
      "index": "CAL:3e547910b451b24656deb217cb5fc163",
